{
  "id": "explore-reading-and-understanding-a-dashboard-collapse-and-expand-a-row",
  "title": "Collapse and expand a row",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "Explore the rows on Demo Wind Farm to see how rows group panels into meaningful sections, how collapsing a row hides its contents, and how the order of the rows forms a logical progression."
    },
    {
      "type": "section",
      "id": "rows",
      "title": "Rows on Demo Wind Farm",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "interactive",
          "action": "navigate",
          "reftarget": "/d/avzwehmz/demo-wind-farm?from=now-12h&to=now&timezone=browser&var-AssetID=e64c9075-9d89-47cb-8ee5-d3251bd253f4",
          "content": "Open the **Demo Wind Farm** dashboard."
        },
        {
          "type": "interactive",
          "action": "highlight",
          "reftarget": "button:has([data-testid='data-testid dashboard-row-title-Wind Farm Power'])",
          "requirements": [
            "on-page:/d/avzwehmz",
            "exists-reftarget"
          ],
          "content": "Focus on the **Wind Farm Power** row heading.",
          "doIt": false,
          "lazyRender": true
        },
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "content": "This row groups a time series panel and a stat panel under one heading, making a meaningful section. A row can hold different types of panels. Its heading tells you what the panels cover before you read them."
        },
        {
          "type": "interactive",
          "action": "highlight",
          "reftarget": "button:has([data-testid='data-testid dashboard-row-title-Wind Farm Power'])",
          "requirements": [
            "on-page:/d/avzwehmz",
            "exists-reftarget"
          ],
          "content": "Select the **Wind Farm Power** arrow to collapse the row."
        },
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "content": "The row's panels are hidden. The heading stays visible so you can expand the row again. Collapsing and expanding rows lets any viewer control what they see."
        },
        {
          "type": "interactive",
          "action": "highlight",
          "reftarget": "button:has([data-testid='data-testid dashboard-row-title-Wind Farm Power'])",
          "requirements": [
            "on-page:/d/avzwehmz",
            "exists-reftarget"
          ],
          "content": "Select the **Wind Farm Power** arrow again to expand the row."
        },
        {
          "type": "interactive",
          "action": "highlight",
          "reftarget": "button:has([data-testid^='data-testid dashboard-row-title-Asset:'])",
          "requirements": [
            "on-page:/d/avzwehmz",
            "exists-reftarget"
          ],
          "content": "Find the row heading that starts with **Asset:**.",
          "doIt": false,
          "lazyRender": true
        },
        {
          "type": "interactive",
          "action": "highlight",
          "reftarget": "div[data-testid^='data-testid dashboard-row-wrapper-for-Asset:']",
          "requirements": [
            "on-page:/d/avzwehmz",
            "exists-reftarget"
          ],
          "content": "Take note that there are five panels using different formats.",
          "doIt": false,
          "lazyRender": true
        },
        {
          "type": "interactive",
          "action": "highlight",
          "reftarget": "button:has([data-testid='data-testid dashboard-row-title-Alerts'])",
          "requirements": [
            "on-page:/d/avzwehmz",
            "exists-reftarget"
          ],
          "content": "Notice the **Alerts** row heading.",
          "doIt": false,
          "lazyRender": true
        },
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "content": "This row holds one panel, an alert list. The three rows form a logical progression: from the wind farm as a whole, to a single asset, to alerts. The layout, where the panels sit and how large they are, follows that order from top to bottom. Panel size and position can help communicate the progression, but you need to read the panel content to understand it."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
